OL,3,GNEWSA'Too hot for ice cream' - summer's
OL,4,Aimpact on trade
OL,5,
OL,6,FAccording to provisional data from the
OL,7,FMet Office, the average mean
OL,8,Ftemperature for June, July and August
OL,9,Fwas 16.5C (61.7F), making it the
OL,10,Fwarmest summer on record in the UK
OL,11,Fbased on statistics stretching back to
OL,12,F1884.
OL,14,FMeteorologists in Jersey and Guernsey
OL,15,Fconfirmed the islands had their warmest
OL,16,Fsummers on record, with average
OL,17,Ftemperatures for Jersey at 20.5C
OL,18,F(68.9F) and 18.9C (66.2F) in Guernsey.
